# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-10). L §3.6 Its split: "rounds to the step by rest largest. Parties whose remainders
# tie go by the owned clause's ties by e ...; a tie with none is refused (RUN-TIE, §5.13)". 100.01 PLN in halves at
# 0.01 leaves one cent that ania and tomek tie for.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
input half: num
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania or p == tomek then half else 0
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania_tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  half = 0.5
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.01 PLN
=== expect
q: (refused: RUN-TIE the split of wage at konto ties at ania, tomek, refused: RUN-TIE the split of wage at konto ties at ania, tomek, refused: RUN-TIE the split of wage at konto ties at ania, tomek, refused: RUN-TIE the split of wage at konto ties at ania, tomek)
  cut 2026-01-01
